[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3866326640","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116026#issuecomment-3866326640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116026","id":3866326640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mc3Zw","user":{"login":"celyk","id":50609684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjA5Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50609684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk","html_url":"https://github.com/celyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-08T06:46:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-08T07:15:52Z","body":"On first thought I didn't like the look of this check\r\n`length(normal_map.xy) > 0.001`\r\n\r\nOn second thought I think it's fine because the intention is to snap the normal. I'm curious to see why this is needed (octahedral compression?).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3866326640/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3867587432","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116026#issuecomment-3867587432","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116026","id":3867587432,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mhrNo","user":{"login":"bugjupiner","id":170782540,"node_id":"U_kgDOCi3vTA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/170782540?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner","html_url":"https://github.com/bugjupiner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-08T17:07:02Z","updated_at":"2026-02-08T17:07:02Z","body":"> On first thought I didn't like the look of this check `length(normal_map.xy) > 0.001`\r\n> \r\n> On second thought I think it's fine because the intention is to snap the normal. I'm curious to see why this is needed (octahedral compression?).\r\n\r\nThe issue is that the tangent/binormal basis orientation varies depending on mesh rotation. \r\n\r\nGenerally, the existing code correctly transforms the normal for each orientation. But when the normal map is flat, the varying tangent basis still causes visible lighting differences between rotated meshes. \r\n\r\nI admit the fix is partial. The deeper issue is that tangent bases can differ between meshes, faces, or UV layouts, which is most apparent on identical geometry. \r\n\r\nInconsistent tangent bases still cause visible differences between adjacent surfaces. A more complete solution might involve recalculating the binormal from the transformed normal/tangent. \r\n\r\nI've posted a GDShader workaround in the original issue for reference.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3867587432/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868357102","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116026#issuecomment-3868357102","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116026","id":3868357102,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mknHu","user":{"login":"celyk","id":50609684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjA5Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50609684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk","html_url":"https://github.com/celyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-08T21:46:03Z","updated_at":"2026-02-08T21:52:20Z","body":"> The deeper issue is that tangent bases can differ between meshes\r\n\r\nSo is the real issue precision? I think if Godot had a high precision option on import the artifact would be reduced.\r\n\r\nI'm also realising that octahedrons have less symmetry than a cube. A 90 degree rotation may not give the same result but a 180 degree rotation should.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868357102/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868419508","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116026#issuecomment-3868419508","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116026","id":3868419508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mk2W0","user":{"login":"bugjupiner","id":170782540,"node_id":"U_kgDOCi3vTA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/170782540?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner","html_url":"https://github.com/bugjupiner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bugjupiner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-08T22:19:19Z","updated_at":"2026-02-08T22:33:55Z","body":"> > The deeper issue is that tangent bases can differ between meshes\r\n> \r\n> So is the real issue precision? I think if Godot had a high precision option on import the artifact would be reduced.\r\n> \r\n> I'm also realising that octahedrons have less symmetry than a cube. A 90 degree rotation may not give the same result but a 180 degree rotation should.\r\n\r\nIf you are able to recreate the steps as stated in Issue #116025 , you'll see that all Y-axis rotations of an identical mesh with an identical material (if Normal Map is enabled) look sharply different than their duplicate.\r\n\r\nIn increments of 90 degrees, both 180 and 270 degrees are still quite visually distinct from one another, mainly any 0 or 360 degree rotation.\r\n\r\nEdit: For easier reference, here's the issue I describe shown in Godot v4.7.dev - Same mesh, same material, just rotated. I discovered these differences while using GridMap to procedurally rotate my \"tiles\" which had materials with Normal Map enabled.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"3536\" height=\"2356\" alt=\"Screenshots\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce6522a7-c823-486e-b879-8d18b6fb94d5\" />\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868419508/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868658008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116026#issuecomment-3868658008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116026","id":3868658008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mlwlY","user":{"login":"celyk","id":50609684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjA5Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50609684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk","html_url":"https://github.com/celyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T00:21:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T00:21:09Z","body":"I've found a better workaround. The imprecision is caused by default normal map being RGB8. The identity normal is (0.5, 0.5, 1.0) but gets quantized to (128, 128, 255), so the value we get in the shader is more like (0.502, 0.502, 1.0). We can account for this by subtracting 0.5 / 255 from the texture sample.\r\n`NORMAL_MAP -= 0.5 / 255.0;`\r\n\r\nThere may still be imprecision introduced by octahedral compression, but it's looking good for cardinal directions.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868658008/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3882153028","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116026#issuecomment-3882153028","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116026","id":3882153028,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nZPRE","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T05:04:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T05:04:30Z","body":"> I've found a better workaround. The imprecision is caused by default normal map being RGB8. The identity normal is (0.5, 0.5, 1.0) but gets quantized to (128, 128, 255), so the value we get in the shader is more like (0.502, 0.502, 1.0). We can account for this by subtracting 0.5 / 255 from the texture sample. `NORMAL_MAP -= 0.5 / 255.0;`\r\n> \r\n> There may still be imprecision introduced by octahedral compression, but it's looking good for cardinal directions.\r\n\r\nVery nice, this approach is much better than using `length()` which is expensive and creating a branch. \r\n\r\nCoincidentally, a similar hack was discussed in this article from last week https://www.ludicon.com/castano/blog/2026/02/normal-map-compression-revisited/","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3882153028/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3882282100","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116026#issuecomment-3882282100","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116026","id":3882282100,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nZux0","user":{"login":"celyk","id":50609684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjA5Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50609684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk","html_url":"https://github.com/celyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T05:41:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T05:41:42Z","body":"Great find! I like that you only need to slightly change the standard formula.\r\n\r\nFor testing I also wrote a script to cycle through all 24 rotations of a cube.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3882282100/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]